      "message": "Let an organisation shape who may do what inside it\n\nWhat being on an organisation means on its repositories is its\nowners' setting. As owners, the default, every member acts as the\nowner of every repository, as before. As readers, members read every\nrepository and make repositories in the organisation's name, and\npushing, reviewing, merging and verifying come from grants the owners\nissue, to a person, an agent, or a team inside the organisation. Such\na team is named under the organisation, org/team, which no principal\nid can look like; it has only the organisation's members on it, holds\ngrants on its repositories, owns nothing and never acts. Being on it\ncarries its grants, only while on the organisation; leaving leaves its\nteams; removing a team revokes what it held. On an organisation's\nrepository its owners grant and revoke, whatever its members do. A\nrepository's settings show who holds what on it and let those who run\nit change that; the organisation's page has its teams and the setting;\neach team has a page. No repository is named teams or members.\n\nTask: t-6a5e933pz868zvrdnjs9myfd23\nChange-Id: Iaccess0126\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
